1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,023
Vocabulary in context is never answered from memory.

2
00:00:04,023 --> 00:00:09,375
Take this sentence, and the question: find a word which means set an upper limit on.

3
00:00:09,375 --> 00:00:13,138
First, read the whole sentence, not the phrase.

4
00:00:13,138 --> 00:00:22,395
Second, fix the part of speech: capped sits between it and the number, so it is a verb in the past tense, and the answer must be a verb.

5
00:00:22,395 --> 00:00:29,687
Third, look for a signal: at four says something was fixed at a maximum, and wary of large groups says why.

6
00:00:29,687 --> 00:00:35,078
Fourth, replace and test: it set an upper limit on the number of guests at four.

7
00:00:35,078 --> 00:00:37,526
It makes sense, so the answer is capped.

8
00:00:37,526 --> 00:00:40,104
The cap you wear on your head is irrelevant.

